        "title": "Mesopotamian Mythology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Mesopotamia (\"land between the rivers\" — Tigris and Euphrates) produced the **oldest written mythology on Earth**. Sumerian cuneiform texts from ~2500 BCE predate Homer by 1,500 years and the Bible by 1,000+. The tradition is layered: Sumerian theology was absorbed, adapted, and transmuted by the Akkadians, then by Babylonians and Assyrians. Same gods, shifting names and dominance hierarchy."
